  "description": "Builds CodeQuery query sources from an existing Entity Framework Core DbContext. The table name, schema and column mapping are read from the EF model, so there is no second schema to maintain: DbSet<T>.ToCodeQuery() hands back a DbTable<T> you can query with CodeQuery's type-safe SQL surface. Reads the EF model only — it scaffolds no migrations and owns no schema.",
